cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "EIV-Core: Execution-Integrity Validator"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hao-Wei
    family-names: Wang
    affiliation: National Taitung University
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USDHGwang/EIV-Core"
abstract: >-
  EIV-Core is an off-chain validator that checks whether an AI agent's on-chain
  transaction stayed within the intent the user signed (an EIP-712 IntentSpec).
  The check is deterministic and uses only the Python standard library,
  including the cryptography. It returns a verdict with the violated
  constraints, can gate a proposed transaction before execution, and can
  record the verdict to an ERC-8004-style validation registry.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - authorization
  - EIP-712
  - ERC-8004
  - signed intent
  - on-chain validation
